WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.630
This is one of the most popular shounen heroes
of all time, and yet for some reason no one

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.300
seems to understand why.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:17.710
So in this video I'm gonna explain exactly
what makes Izuku such a fantastic protagonist.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:27.470
Midoriya, or as his kind and not at all abusive
childhood-friend Bakugo called him, Deku,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:34.059
a nickname for someone who can't do anything,
is a surprisingly controversial main character

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:35.089
for many people.

00:00:35.089 --> 00:00:42.870
While he ticks of an impressive number of
Shounen tropes, like his unique power, his

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.949
tragic childhood or his constant strive to
up his abilities, Deku also gives of a way

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:53.719
more vulnerable, insecure and feminine vibe
than most typical shounen heroes, even though

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:58.329
all, or at least most of them, share similar
insecurities.

00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:06.470
Deku however, despite wielding the strongest
quirk in the story, is surprisingly open about

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:11.280
these insecurities, as well as his emotions
and his generally empathetic nature.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:17.290
And it's this twist on the stereotypical hard-boiled,
tough guy protagonist who buries all negative

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:22.570
thoughts and emotions deep within himself,
that seems to give Midoriya a bad reputation

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.390
with some anime and manga fans.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:29.110
And yet, it's exactly this openness about
his own feelings and weaknesses, that make

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:33.980
Deku and his journey to becoming the greatest
hero of all time a story that is more than

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.560
worth following along.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:40.970
It's a story about growth, both on a personal
level AND on the level of society, making

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:45.600
Boku no hero way more complex and deep than
it appears to be on the surface.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.580
And so, to understand what makes Deku a fantastic
main character, we will look at his personality

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:57.100
and story arc, his major flaw as a character
as well as his relationships with Bakugo and

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:01.140
Tomura and how both shape the story around
him.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:18.980
This is the story of Midoriya Izuku.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.290
The first thing you need to do, if you want
to understand any character in a story, is

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:28.640
figure out what the central theme, the central
moral argument of said story is, that the

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.400
author tries to convey through the characters
and the plot.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.290
What's the take home message, when we are
done?

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:40.370
In the case of Boku no Hero hero, after over
300 chapters, it is quite clear, that the

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:46.430
central moral question that Horikoshi is exploring,
is both surprisingly basic and complex at

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:55.270
the same time: What does it mean to be a great
hero?

00:02:55.270 --> 00:03:00.250
Duh.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.490
But this question implies a lot more than
you might think.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:09.160
Because the story explores this problem, by
contrasting two polar viewpoints, individualism

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.580
and collectivism.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.930
In other words, what does it mean to be a
great hero on a personal level and what does

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:23.330
it mean to be a great hero from the viewpoint
of society.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:27.860
Right from the start, we are told that Midoriya
wants to become the greatest hero, that saves

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:28.860
everybody.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:35.040
A statement, so vague and so shounen, that
I'm 95% sure Hirokoshi chose it on purpose,

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.290
so he could put his own twists on it.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:42.400
At the same time, We get introduced to this
society, that similarly seems to be as straightforward

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:48.760
and simple as it gets: The peaceful citizens
are protected by the good heroes from the

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:54.410
bad villains, paining this quirk society as
a peaceful utopia, only that everyone has

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:59.930
superpowers.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:04.820
And despite everyone having a unique superpower,
this society is normal.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.020
When everyone's special, no one is special.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:13.849
And when you think about it for a second,
the wording Horikoshi chose here is also very

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:14.849
clever.

00:04:14.849 --> 00:04:20.049
a story about heroes and villains, sets our
expectations for these groups as starkly as

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:25.600
humanly possible, especially as in the first
couple of arcs, both groups fulfill these

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:29.000
expectations perfectly.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:38.560
Villains do bad things and the heroes stop
them to save and protect everyone.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.680
And yet it doesn't take all too long, until
you realize that this initial black and white

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:47.970
view of the Boku No hero world, is not reality,
but we are literally sharing Midoriya's faulty

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.000
worldview for a large part of the story.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.330
Midoriya thinks that being a great hero, means
saving people being assaulted by bad villains,

00:04:56.330 --> 00:05:08.150
that cause all the pain and suffering in this
otherwise perfect society.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:14.020
His major flaw as a character is his fanatic
idealization of the hero world, that is projected

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:23.670
on the number one hero all might, that Midoriya
almost worships like a god.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.460
So, why exactly does Deku think that way?

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:32.000
While in general, society itself seems to
propagate this simplified image of good and

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.340
evil as well, the deeper answer can be found
with the Deuteragonist of the story.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:43.440
Deku has endured verbal and physical abuse
from Bakugo for over 10 years.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:47.090
He's 15 now, that means for over 2 thirds
of his life.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:51.540
In this society that is shaped and defined
by quirks and that lives under the guard of

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:57.660
the hero profession, Deku is one of the rare
cases where a quirk has not manifested.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:01.850
In other words, he's a normal human being,
like you and me.

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:06.919
*Which makes him relatable* Only that in this
society of superpowers, this makes him the

00:06:06.919 --> 00:06:13.640
true outcast.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:19.020
Being a very kind-hearted and altruistic person
by nature, that wants to help people, having

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.509
no quirk put so much distance between him
and his dream of becoming a hero, that Deku

00:06:24.509 --> 00:06:29.590
had no other choice but to either completely
idolize or detest them.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:34.590
The fact that Bakugo kept treating him like
a piece of trash for not owning a quirk, manifested

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:39.800
such a strong sense of low self-worth and
insecurity within him, that when he finally

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:45.640
got the chance to become a hero against all
odds, he embraced this one thing he always

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:57.860
wanted as all good and all powerful, completely
incapable of seeing it's flaws.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:03.310
Even after Bakugo stopped constantly picking
on Deku, you still see him twitching and stuttering

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:07.630
whenever he is around him, again and again
taking away from the confidence that Midoriya

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:13.509
slowly builds over time by mastering one for
all and fighting for and with his friends.

00:07:13.509 --> 00:07:19.090
I believe this is quite often overlooked,
but as he says himself in this panel here,

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.520
Midoriya truly hates Bakugo.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.419
He admires him, ever since they were young,
yes.

00:07:24.419 --> 00:07:27.070
But he hates him for the way he treated him.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:32.230
And it is the low sense of self-worth that
Bakugo beat into him over and over and over

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:37.810
and over, that makes Deku blind to the reality
around him, idolizing the hero profession

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:42.850
so much, that he keeps putting his health
and life on the line to such an absolutly

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:54.910
ridiculous and unhealthy extend that it quickly
becomes worrying to everyone around him.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:59.050
And so, while the impulsive and egocentric
Bakugo has to learn to be more considerate

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:04.210
of others, something that I will discuss in
detail in his analysis, the neurotic and altruistic

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:09.520
Midoriya has to learn to respect himself more
and make harder decisions, in order to actually

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.380
be able to save others.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:17.690
A great example of this insight beginning
to dawn on him, is when Izuku can't save Bakugo,

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:27.699
as he has already sacrificed both his arms.

00:08:27.699 --> 00:08:32.130
For the longest time, proving himself to be
worthy of inheriting one for all and becoming

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:38.789
a hero is more important to him than his own
well-being, even if it means being less effective

00:08:38.789 --> 00:08:39.950
and useful.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:46.740
Now, while Midoria's need for self-realization
and maturity is quite evident early on, the

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:52.810
story takes a while to reveal the other aspect
of Midoria's flaw, the ambiguous and dark

00:08:52.810 --> 00:09:03.120
side of the hero society.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.200
However more and more, you learn that this
world, where good heroes save the innocent

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.850
citizens from the evil villains is a lot more
morally gray and complex, than you originally

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:13.850
thought.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.181
As so often is the case with apparent utopias
in stories, it turns out, that it's the hero

00:09:18.181 --> 00:09:23.490
society itself that produces its villains
in the first place, as, big surprise, most

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:30.060
people aren't born evil, but become who they
are as the result of their circumstances.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:34.990
Yes there is also some exploration of the
concepts nature vs. nurture in boku no hero,

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:42.420
but primarily, Horikoshi focuses on external
circumstances.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:46.920
Exploring what makes people into villains,
is a major aspect of the story, that is explored

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:51.410
in a number of ways, going as far as making
the villains the main characters of certain

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:52.410
story arcs.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:10:00.040
And the central symbol for this all, is none
other than Shigaraki Tomura, the anti Deku,

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:06.260
whom we follow on HIS path to becoming the
strongest villain.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:12.950
Firstly, we understand that in this society
of quirks, there are two very fundamental

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:13.950
flaws.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.680
Both of them are explored over and over again.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:21.440
The first of these is the notion that people
with destructive or dangerous quirks are treated

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.880
as outcasts and incompatible with society.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:30.370
This of course is a pretty straightforward
metaphor for general racism in the real world.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:36.120
Discrimination based on physical attributes,
one has absolutely no control over.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:43.190
No matter if it's Tomura, Dabi or Twice, at
some point we get that these people don'T

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:48.870
have terrible quirks because they are villains,
no, they are villains because they have horrible

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:49.870
quirks.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:56.390
A fantastic example for this is Eri, who mirrors
Tomura's story almost completely with the

00:10:56.390 --> 00:11:02.250
exception that the heroes actually end up
saving her, as they failed to do with Tomura.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:08.050
The second flaw of the hero society is that
the profession of heroes, that is far beyond

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:13.430
all good and noble, additionally has eradicated
the common sense of compassion and altruism

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:18.630
in the society at large.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:21.880
This point is especially pronounced in Tomura's
backstory.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:26.900
Instead of helping the lost child, people
simply assume that some heroes will do the

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.660
job, not bothering to do anything themselves.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:36.010
Thus ultimately, it's the society of heroes
themselves that creates most of these villains,

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:57.090
by failing to do what Midoriya idealizes about
them, saving everyone.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:12:02.829
This is interesting, because Midoriya and
Tomura of course mirror each other extremely

00:12:02.829 --> 00:12:07.900
closely, with Deku himself being a victim
of discrimination and neglect, only that he

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:12.700
gets taken in by the hero all might, while
Tomura gets taken in by One for all.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:16.100
Don't forget that Tomura wanted to be a hero
too.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:22.470
And yet Midoriya is only starting to recognize
very very slowly, this truth about the world,

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:28.750
that the society of heroes that he has thought
to be perfect, is not so perfect after all.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:34.279
And that brings me to Deku's character arc,
and what actually makes him a true hero, even

00:12:34.279 --> 00:12:36.970
if it takes quite a while in the story to
get there.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:45.280
The payoff however is just the better.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:50.660
As a result of these two character flaws,
no self worth and blinding idealization of

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:56.460
the hero world, what emerges only very slowly,
but very clearly throughout the story, is

00:12:56.460 --> 00:13:01.839
that Midoriya's arc is about understanding
the complexity and faults of society while

00:13:01.839 --> 00:13:07.370
at the same time growing past his personal
flaws to truly become a hero that can save

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:13.279
everyone, even, no, especially someone as
apparently un-redeemable as Tomura, who by

00:13:13.279 --> 00:13:17.370
mere chance was forced to take the path opposite
to Izuku.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.180
And this arc is in full progress now.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:24.470
Especially in his more recent encounters with
Tomura, Midoriya is starting to to see the

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:29.860
world for what it is, yes heroes help and
are important to keep the balance in a world

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:44.150
full of dangerous superpowers, but the system
is neither perfect nor unfailable.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:48.610
Similarly he is starting to grow as a person,
as with the mastering of his abilities and

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:53.769
all the set-backs he had from going over-board
with his self-sacrificial attitude, he has

00:13:53.769 --> 00:14:00.100
started to mature, fight smarter, thinks about
himself more and overall starts to form his

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:05.640
own opinions and believes about what it means
to be good hero.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:12.550
This slow emancipation from all might and
the other heroes he always admired is important.

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:15.300
Imitation is a strong theme within the story.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:20.860
Over and over, we are shown that trying to
be exactly like someone always leads to tragedy

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:25.459
and failure.

00:14:25.459 --> 00:14:33.779
Instead, Horikoshi promotes the idea, that
taking inspiration from those you admire is

00:14:33.779 --> 00:14:38.850
great, as long as you walk your own path and
find your own way of doing things.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:43.550
We see this with Iida, who tries to be like
his brother, Todoroki and his mother, Twice

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:49.820
and his clones and of course Deku and Bakugo
who both try to imitate their respective ideal

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:50.820
of all might.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:56.230
No matter which of the the countless examples
you take, they always end in failure.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:15:10.860
Imitating someone else, brings suffering,
not 

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:11.860
self-realization.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:16.010
Ironically enough, it is Deku's incredibly
pure and straightforward character, that changes

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:20.140
the mind of many of these people, Iida, Todoroki,
ect.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:24.620
And finally, Deku also starts to realize this
more and more.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:28.950
All might wasn't perfect, as he also couldn't
save everyone.

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:34.649
Instead Deku starts going his own path, unlocking
new powers of one for all, while realizing,

00:15:34.649 --> 00:15:39.800
that saving everyone also includes those that
the current society has abandoned.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:44.940
The kick off to this development is this moment
here, where Midoriya realizes that instead

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:52.650
of punching like all might, it might suit
him way better to kick.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:16:00.500
And so, in the end, it's Deku's genuine goodness
and desire to help others and improve the

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:04.160
life of those around him, his immeasurable
courage and ability to change the hearts of

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:07.450
those around him, that make him a true hero.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:12.290
And while it might be frustrating at first
to follow him as a protagonist who starts

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:18.540
form a very negative point on his character
arc, the more the story and Deku progress,

